From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] infra/hosts/beastie: Make the list's folders before the
 first sync
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab@lists.p7x.dev
Change-Id: znykxnkkkmrroutoxzqntqylulozmouy
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:37:42 +0000

mbsync dumped core on beastie on its first sync into a mail root that
held only sent, though Create Near should have made the list's
folders. Making INBOX, Next, Later, and Archive in just install-mail
means the first sync finds every folder it expects.
---
change-id: znykxnkkkmrroutoxzqntqylulozmouy

 infra/hosts/beastie/README.org              |  6 ++++--
 infra/hosts/beastie/libexec/install-mail.sh | 12 ++++++++----
 jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org           |  7 ++++---
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/infra/hosts/beastie/README.org b/infra/hosts/beastie/README.org
index d2bd8e4e..a59777df 100644
--- a/infra/hosts/beastie/README.org
+++ b/infra/hosts/beastie/README.org
@@ -25,8 +25,10 @@ three layers, from most shared to most specific:
 
    =just install-mail= installs them, and keeps any installed file
    that differs as =<file>.old=. It also makes the mail root,
-   =~/mail/pat@p7x.dev=, with the =sent= folder that mbsync never
-   syncs.
+   =~/mail/pat@p7x.dev=, with the list's folders, INBOX, =Next=,
+   =Later=, and =Archive=, and the =sent= folder that mbsync never
+   syncs. mbsync dumped core on beastie on a first sync into folders
+   that did not exist.
 
 ** password
 mbsync reads the password of =pat@p7x.dev= on lab-mail from
diff --git a/infra/hosts/beastie/libexec/install-mail.sh b/infra/hosts/beastie/libexec/install-mail.sh
index ce1f4568..12625034 100755
--- a/infra/hosts/beastie/libexec/install-mail.sh
+++ b/infra/hosts/beastie/libexec/install-mail.sh
@@ -4,9 +4,9 @@
 # it as Pat, as just install-mail. The repo holds the config, so an
 # installed file that differs is replaced and kept as <file>.old.
 #
-# It also makes the mail root's sent folder, which mbsync never syncs,
-# and an empty password file for Pat to fill in. It never changes a
-# password file that exists.
+# It also makes the mail root's folders, the list's and the sent
+# folder that mbsync never syncs, and an empty password file for Pat to
+# fill in. It never changes a password file that exists.
 set -eu
 
 src="$(dirname "$(realpath "$0")")/../mail"
@@ -20,7 +20,11 @@ install -b -C -m 0644 "${src}/notmuch-config" \
 install -b -C -m 0600 "${src}/mbsyncrc" "${HOME}/.mbsyncrc"
 install -b -C -m 0600 "${src}/msmtprc" "${HOME}/.msmtprc"
 
-install -d "${root}/sent/cur" "${root}/sent/new" "${root}/sent/tmp"
+# mbsync dumped core on beastie on a first sync into folders that did
+# not exist, though Create Near should make them.
+for box in INBOX Next Later Archive sent; do
+	install -d "${root}/${box}/cur" "${root}/${box}/new" "${root}/${box}/tmp"
+done
 
 install -d -m 0700 "${pwdir}"
 if [ ! -e "${pwfile}" ]; then
diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org b/jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org
index d2deeaad..4f626269 100644
--- a/jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org
@@ -270,9 +270,10 @@ up the same way and differ only in the login.
   itself; each host installs its own, with its login. lab-claude
   ships its own and documents them in its README.
 - On beastie, =infra/hosts/beastie/mail= holds Pat's configs, and
-  =just install-mail= there installs them, makes the mail root, and
-  makes an empty password file for Pat to fill in. beastie's README
-  documents the setup, from the ports to the password.
+  =just install-mail= there installs them, makes the mail root and
+  its folders, and makes an empty password file for Pat to fill in.
+  beastie's README documents the setup, from the ports to the
+  password.
 - The agent searches and reads the local index, not IMAP.
 - On beastie, Emacs reads the profile and posts through msmtp. It
   saves each message it posts by Fcc into =sent=, so the message shows
